| Total sales (فروش کل) | `GET /api/admin/stats` | `Order.aggregate([{$match: {status: {$ne: "cancelled"}}}, {$group: {_id: null, total: {$sum: "$totalAmount"}}}]`) | ❌ None — sums ALL non-cancelled orders |
| Total orders (سفارشات) | `GET /api/admin/stats` | `Order.countDocuments({})` | ❌ None |
| Pending orders | `GET /api/admin/stats` | `Order.countDocuments({ status: "pending_payment" })` | ❌ None |
| Products (محصولات) | `GET /api/admin/stats` | `Product.countDocuments({})` | ❌ None — counts ALL products regardless of `isActive` |
| Users (کاربران) | `GET /api/admin/stats` | `User.countDocuments({})` | ❌ None — counts ALL users regardless of `isActive` |
| Recent orders (آخرین سفارشات) | `GET /api/admin/orders?page=1&limit=5` | `Order.find({}).populate("customer").sort({createdAt: -1}).limit(5)` | ❌ None — shows ALL orders |

### 1.2 Why `نامشخص` (Unknown) appears (VERIFIED from source)

In `src/app/api/admin/orders/route.ts` (line 102):
```ts
Order.find(filter).populate("customer", "name phone")
```

In `src/app/admin/dashboard/page.tsx` (line 61):
```tsx
customer: order.customer?.name || "نامشخص"
```

`نامشخص` appears when **any** of these is true:
1. The `customer` ObjectId on the order references a user document that was **deleted** from the `users` collection (orphaned order)
2. The `customer` field on the order is `null` or missing
3. The referenced user exists but has an empty/falsy `name`

This is **not** a dashboard serialization bug — it is the expected fallback when the customer reference cannot be resolved.

### 1.3 Why records remain visible after Phase 2

**VERIFIED:** Phase 2 was strictly read-only. No deletion, update, or restore was ever executed. The dashboard/API queries contain **zero test-data filtering**, so every record created during testing remains visible in:
- Admin dashboard stats (total users, products, orders, revenue, growth)
- Admin orders list
- Admin reports (sales, orders, payments, refunds, coupons, customers, inventory, P&L, accounting)
- Storefront (if product has `isActive: true` and `stock > 0`)

The Phase 2 candidate manifest was **prepared but never executed**, and it focused on backup-string patterns rather than the live dashboard-visible records identified here.

